ents stock on success\n   - release → increments stock back\n   - setLowStockThreshold → sets threshold for alert\n   - Low stock: when stock changes to at or below threshold, emit LOW_STOCK_ALERT\n\n   For low stock check: after any stock change (set/remove/release), check if current <= threshold, emit alert.\n\n3. **Cart**:\n   - createCart → returns cartId (UUID)\n   - addItem → if product exists, increment quantity; emit CART_UPDATED\n   - removeItem → if product doesn't exist, still emit CART_UPDATED (or not?)\n   - getCart → null if cart doesn't exist\n   - clearCart → remove all items; emit CART_UPDATED\n   - updateQuantity → set specific qty; if 0 or negative, maybe remove? emit CART_UPDATED\n\n   For CART_UPDATED payload: CartUpdatedEvent has cartId, userId, items array.\n\n4. **Pricing**:\n   - calculateTotal → compute all the values\n   - addDiscountCode → register code\n   - getPrice → from stored product prices\n   - On PRODUCT_CREATED: store price\n\n5. **Orders**:\n   - createOrder → generate UUID, store with PENDING status, emit ORDER_CREATED\n   - getOrder → null if not found\n   - updateStatus → validate lifecycle; emit ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED\n   - listOrders → filter by userId\n\n6. **Payment**:\n   - processPayment → async, simulate based on options\n   - refund → try to refund transaction\n   - Emit PAYMENT_PROCESSED\n\n7. **Notifications**:\n   - subscribe → add user (track user)\n   - getNotifications → return list\n   - Listen for ORDER_CREATED: store orderId→userId mapping\n   - Listen for ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED: create notification for user\n   - Listen for PAYMENT_PROCESSED: create notification for user\n\n8. **Analytics**:\n   - Listen for all events → count events\n   - Listen for PAYMENT_PROCESSED success → revenue\n   - Listen for ORDER_CREATED → count orders\n   - Listen for CART_UPDATED → unique carts, store items\n   - When ORDER_CREATED → look up cart items for product counts\n\nLet me also think about how the analytics service gets th