+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"d044cb85-93a2-4538-a084-87968c1eef64","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me also check the notification service. The notification test had a notification test that passed but the integration test had an issue. Let me look at the integration test failure:\n\n```\nFull Checkout Flow Integration > runs a complete order lifecycle end-to-end\nAssertionError: expected 0 to be greater than or equal to 2\n```\n\nLet me check that test:\n```typescript\n// 8. Check notifications\nnotifications.subscribe('alice');\n// Since notifications already listened to events from steps 5-7,\n// alice should have notifications\nconst notes = notifications.getNotifications('alice');\nexpect(notes.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);\n```\n\nThe issue: `notifications.subscribe('alice')` is called AFTER the events have been emitted. So the service didn't capture any notifications because Alice wasn't subscribed.\n\nWait, but let me look at the notification service more carefully:\n\n```typescript\nbus.on(Events.ORDER_CREATED, (payload: unknown) => {\n  const event = payload as OrderCreatedEvent;\n  orderOwners.set(event.orderId, event.userId);\n});\n```\n\nThis handler runs for ALL ORDER_CREATED events regardless of subscription. It just records the orderId->userId mapping. That's fine.\n\n```typescript\nfunction addNotification(userId: string, type: string, message: string): void {\n  if (!subscriptions.has(userId)) return;\n  ...\n}\n\nbus.on(Events.ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED, (payload: unknown) => {\n  const event = payload as OrderStatusChangedEvent;\n  const userId = orderOwners.get(event.orderId);\n  if (userId) {\n    addNotification(userId, 'order_status', `Order ${event.orderId} changed from ${event.previousStatus} to ${event.status}`);\n  }\n});\n```\n\nThe ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED handler checks `orderOwners` to find the userId. Then calls `addNotification` which checks subscription. If the user isn't subscribed, it returns without adding.\n\nSo in the integration test:\n1. Events fire in steps 5-7 (order created, payment processed, status changes)\n2. The notification service records orderOwners for ORDER_CREATED\n3. But when ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED and PAYMENT_PROCESSED fire, Alice isn't subscribed yet\n4. Later, `notifications.subscribe('alice')` is called, but the events already fired\n\nSo I need to move the subscribe call earlier in the integration test. Let me fix that.\n\nAlso, let me reconsider the notification test itself:\n\n```typescript\nit('records notification on order status change', () => {\n  notifications.subscribe('user1');\n  const orderId = orders.createOrder('user1', 'cart1', 50);\n  orders.updateStatus(orderId, OrderStatus.CONFIRMED);\n  ...\n});\n```\n\nHere, `subscribe` is called BEFORE the events. So the test passes because:\n1. ORDER_CREATED handler records orderOwners. The addNotification checks subscription but ORDER_CREATED only sets orderOwners, it doesn't add notifications.\n2. ORDER_STATUS_CHANGED handler looks up userId from orderOwners, calls addNotification which checks subscription — user1 IS subscribed.\n\nSo the notification test should pass. But the integration test needs to subscribe before the events.\n\nLet me fix the integration test.","signature":"d044cb85-93a2-4538-a084-87968c1eef64"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":139,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":57344,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d53b0a8a-1c2b-4d75-a516-3b1b90cc6b06","uuid":"529bbc67-0967-4d4a-b99a-99312e32d65d"}
